*> OBIC1A -- obsolete-language CALL test from the NIST COBOL-85 suite. It
*> CALLs two subprograms: OBIC2A (USING SORT-LINK) and OBIC3A (USING the
*> print-line values). Both are mocked here, one per test case, so neither
*> subprogram module has to be present or compiled.
TESTSUITE "OBIC1A CALL statement tests"

TESTCASE "CALL-IC219 calls subprogram OBIC2A (mocked)"
    MOCK CALL "OBIC2A"
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM CALL-IC219
    VERIFY CALL "OBIC2A" WAS CALLED ONCE

TESTCASE "CALL-FAIL calls subprogram OBIC3A (mocked)"
    MOCK CALL "OBIC3A"
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM CALL-FAIL
    VERIFY CALL "OBIC3A" WAS CALLED AT LEAST ONCE
